    description: "FOUND by WI-tusad F3 (analogue sweep for \"qualified_name keeps only the innermost scope\", fixed for C#, TypeScript and Tcl in PR #1571). Python sets qualified_name equal to the emitted name: a method of a nested class is `B.go` with qualified_name `B.go`, not `A.B.go` (PEP 3155 __qualname__), and the nested class `B` has qualified_name `B`. py.py documents this as deliberate (\"v6 is a stable_id-only change; the field's scope-qualification (and its call-resolution effects) is separate work\"); stable_ids already hash the full chain. This item is that separate work: decide whether Python qualified_name follows __qualname__ (and module path), and measure the call-resolution effect first. Probe: scratchpad fixes/f3/qn/probe.py."  # 6fd0
    fields: {}  # 6fd0
